<title>FRANCE: EU cuts maize import tariffs to Spain, Portugal. [CORRECTED 18:05 GMT]</title>
<headline>EU cuts maize import tariffs to Spain, Portugal. [CORRECTED 18:05 GMT]</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-02-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>The European Union on Thursday awarded a tariff cut of 60.98 Ecus per tonne for imports of 569,000 tonnes of maize to Spain, France's ONIC said.</p>
<p>It also cut the tariff by 51.99 Ecus per tonne for imports of 269,000 tonnes of maize to Portugal, it said.</p>
<p>The EU's grain panel in Brussels also agreed a tariff cut of 38.45 Ecus per tonne for imports of 79,000 tonnes of sorghum to Spain. (Corrects country from &quot;Portugal&quot;. French cereals office ONIC said it erroneously reported Portugal as the destination instead of Spain in a published note)</p>
<p>The tariff cuts are for preferential imports of grain from the United States under EU accession agreements struck in 1987.</p>
</text>
